{
  "_comment": "Save this as .mcp.json at the root of each project repo and commit it -- UNLESS you set a real QDRANT_API_KEY below (see that field's own note), in which case do NOT commit this file as-is; keep it out of version control for this project instead. Change COLLECTION_NAME per project. Opening Claude Code in a project directory loads that project's .mcp.json automatically, so switching projects switches collections with zero manual action. REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON: substitute the absolute path to the Python interpreter inside the tools-repo virtual environment (e.g. /home/youruser/tools/claude-runway/.venv/bin/python) -- using a plain 'python' here fails on Linux because the MCP servers need packages installed in that venv. All the servers use the same venv Python, and each runs one of this repo's own scripts (mcpservers/qdrant_mcp_server.py, mcpservers/ingest_mcp_server.py, mcpservers/memory_bank_mcp_server.py, mcpservers/compress_mcp_server.py and, opt-in, mcpservers/analytics_mcp_server.py and mcpservers/codebase_reviewer_mcp_server.py). MEMORY_BANK_COLLECTION (codebase-indexer and memory-bank blocks) is the ONE collection every project's memory-bank server shares -- see the memory-bank block's own _comment. INDEX_INCLUDE_EXTENSIONS/INDEX_EXCLUDE_DIRS are optional -- leave blank ('') to use the built-in code/doc extension list and default excludes (.git, node_modules, dist, build, etc.) plus the repo's own .gitignore. Set INDEX_INCLUDE_EXTENSIONS (e.g. '.py,.md') to restrict to specific file types, or INDEX_EXCLUDE_DIRS (e.g. 'fixtures,generated') to skip additional folders. COLLECTION_DESCRIPTION is optional -- leave blank ('') for no static hint, or set a short one-line description of what this collection contains; applied automatically to the collection's Qdrant metadata at server startup and after index_repo/sync_repo write, so list_collections (from a DIFFERENT project's session) can surface it without anyone having to call set_collection_description by hand. QDRANT_API_KEY (present in the qdrant, codebase-indexer and memory-bank env blocks) is optional -- leave blank ('') for an unauthenticated local Qdrant instance, or set it to your API key for an authenticated remote one; the same variable name qdrant_mcp_server.py/ingest_mcp_server.py/memory_bank_mcp_server.py all read, so one value keeps every Qdrant-talking server in this file aligned. WARNING if you DO set a real key: this file is otherwise meant to be committed (see the top of this comment), so a real QDRANT_API_KEY here would publish that credential in plaintext to anyone with repo access, permanently in git history even after a later edit -- there's no built-in mechanism here for loading it from an untracked source instead, so keep .mcp.json itself out of version control for this project (add it to .gitignore) or manage the key through your own separate, untracked process.",

  "mcpServers": {
    "qdrant": {
      "_comment": "This repo's own server: qdrant-find and qdrant-store (this project's COLLECTION_NAME) plus compact_store, compact_find and compact_prune (the conversation compacts /my-compact and /my-resume use, under COMPACT_COLLECTION plus the project name). EMBEDDING_MODEL is the code-index model and must match the codebase-indexer block. COMPACT_EMBEDDING_MODEL is the model conversation compacts are embedded with, deliberately separate: compacts are stored under a model-named vector, so changing it for an install that already has compacts orphans them -- leave it alone once /my-compact has been used (installs that predate this setting are pinned to BAAI/bge-small-en by `upgrade`). CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_URL/CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_MODEL are used only by compact_store, which compresses the summary through the local model before storing it and stores it uncompressed if LM Studio is unavailable (blank CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_MODEL auto-detects the loaded model). They are read from THIS env block, not a shell export. Leave QDRANT_API_KEY empty for unauthenticated local Qdrant; if you DO set a real key, see the top-level _comment's warning about not committing this file as-is.",
      "command": "REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON",
      "type": "stdio",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcpservers/qdrant_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": {
        "QDRANT_URL": "http://localhost:6333",
        "QDRANT_API_KEY": "",
        "COLLECTION_NAME": "REPLACE-WITH-THIS-PROJECTS-NAME",
        "EMBEDDING_MODEL": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
        "COMPACT_COLLECTION": "conversation-compacts",
        "COMPACT_EMBEDDING_MODEL": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
        "CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_URL": "http://localhost:1234/v1",
        "CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_MODEL": "REPLACE-WITH-MODEL"
      }
    },
    "codebase-indexer": {
      "command": "REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON",
      "type": "stdio",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcpservers/ingest_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": {
        "QDRANT_URL": "http://localhost:6333",
        "QDRANT_API_KEY": "",
        "COLLECTION_NAME": "REPLACE-WITH-THIS-PROJECTS-NAME",
        "COLLECTION_DESCRIPTION": "",
        "EMBEDDING_MODEL": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
        "INDEX_INCLUDE_EXTENSIONS": "",
        "INDEX_EXCLUDE_DIRS": "",
        "MEMORY_BANK_COLLECTION": "memory-bank"
      }
    },
    "memory-bank": {
      "_comment": "MEMORY_BANK_ID is a plain identifier for THIS project -- every memory it writes gets tagged with this value, so recall/forget default to just this project's own memories (with an explicit override to look at another project's). It doesn't have to match any real Qdrant collection name; set it to whatever uniquely identifies this project. MEMORY_BANK_COLLECTION is a different thing entirely: the ONE shared Qdrant collection (default 'memory-bank') every project's memories are actually stored in, common to every project on this Qdrant instance. EMBEDDING_MODEL here is memory-bank's OWN model, independent of the qdrant/codebase-indexer blocks' EMBEDDING_MODEL: it MUST match whatever model created that shared collection (whichever project got there first), and every project sharing it needs to agree on this value -- a mismatch is detected and reported clearly. Change it only deliberately (setup_project.py init --memory-bank-embedding-model), as it breaks remember/recall for every project until the collection is rebuilt. See templates/CLAUDE.md.template's 'Durable memory' section for the full design.",
      "command": "REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON",
      "type": "stdio",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcpservers/memory_bank_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": {
        "QDRANT_URL": "http://localhost:6333",
        "QDRANT_API_KEY": "",
        "MEMORY_BANK_ID": "ANY-NAME-YOU-WANT",
        "MEMORY_BANK_COLLECTION": "memory-bank",
        "EMBEDDING_MODEL": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
      }
    },
    "local-compress": {
      "_comment": "This server does not use Qdrant: the conversation-compact tools moved to the qdrant server. CLAUDE_RUNWAY_TRACK_SAVINGS is optional (opt-in savings tracker, off by default; accepts '1', 'true', or 'yes', case-insensitive and whitespace-trimmed -- anything else, including unset/empty, is off): when on, this server returns each compressed result inside a small JSON envelope (the text plus its size metrics) that the hook unwraps and records, so restart Claude Code after upgrading the server and the hook together. CLAUDE_RUNWAY_SAVINGS_DB does not belong here: this server never opens the savings database (the hooks write it and the analytics server reads it), so an override goes in the analytics block and the shell export, and `upgrade` removes a leftover copy from this block. Setting CLAUDE_RUNWAY_TRACK_SAVINGS HERE is still the reliable way to guarantee this server sees them: a stdio MCP server subprocess actually inherits the ENTIRE parent shell environment (not a small fixed allowlist — verified directly, see README's 'Why two places' section), with this env block layered on top, added/overriding rather than filtering. But you can't always guarantee `claude` was launched from a shell that already ran a given export (a GUI launcher, a different profile, another machine) — so a custom var merely exported in your shell isn't reliably visible to this server across every launch context unless it's also listed explicitly in this env block, same as any other MCP server config. (This describes Claude Code's own observed subprocess behavior, verified directly -- not something the MCP spec itself mandates; a different MCP client could construct or filter a stdio server's environment differently, so treat this as specific to Claude Code rather than a universal MCP guarantee.) Separately, compress_output.py / session_end_savings.py (hook scripts, not MCP servers) need the SAME values exported at the shell level too — hooks have the opposite problem: no env block of their own in settings.json, so they only ever see what's in the shell environment. See settings.json.template's _savings_tracker_note.",
      "command": "REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON",
      "type": "stdio",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcpservers/compress_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": {
        "CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_URL": "http://localhost:1234/v1",
        "CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_MODEL": "REPLACE-WITH-MODEL",
        "CLAUDE_RUNWAY_TRACK_SAVINGS": ""
      }
    },
    "analytics": {
      "_comment": "OPTIONAL: delete this block unless you track savings. `init --track-savings` writes it; without that flag it is not written. It serves savings_summary, savings_detail, savings_trend, get_metrics and record_metric, which read the savings database and the shared metrics database. It needs only the `mcp` package: no embedding model, no LM Studio and no Qdrant. Recording does not go through it: the local-compress server returns the metrics and the hooks write the events, regardless. Without this block those five tools do not exist, which means an unknown-tool error, not empty data. CLAUDE_RUNWAY_SAVINGS_DB and CLAUDE_RUNWAY_METRICS_DB are written by `init` only when overridden (add them here by hand if you use a non-default location; a blank value masks an inherited shell value rather than falling back to the default). `init --metrics-db` also writes CLAUDE_RUNWAY_METRICS_DB into the memory-bank block, which writes its call tally into the same metrics database; a hand edit has to change both.",
      "command": "REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON",
      "type": "stdio",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcpservers/analytics_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": {
        "CLAUDE_RUNWAY_TRACK_SAVINGS": "1"
      }
    },
    "codebase-reviewer": {
      "_comment": "OPTIONAL: delete this block unless you use the local review loop. `init --codebase-reviewer` writes it (`upgrade` offers it); without that it is not written. REVIEWERS_FILE is REQUIRED and has NO default: set it to the path of your own reviewers JSON file (the models, prompts and rubric are entirely yours; this toolkit ships none and never writes a default path or a default file). A blank, missing, unreadable or invalid file is an error at run time that names the file and what is wrong, and no review runs; `claude-runway-doctor` reports it too. MAX_REVIEWERS is how many reviewers run at once (\"1\" runs them one at a time); size it to your machine and to LM Studio's Max Concurrent Predictions. MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS is the most rounds of Copilot feedback an unattended run goes through before a human is brought in. QDRANT_URL/QDRANT_API_KEY are for the scoring database (a later piece of work); leave QDRANT_API_KEY empty for an unauthenticated local Qdrant (see the top-level _comment's warning about a real key). The LM Studio URL is not written here: the server reads CLAUDE_RUNWAY_LMSTUDIO_URL from the shell like the other servers do.",
      "command": "REPLACE-WITH-VENV-PYTHON",
      "type": "stdio",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/mcpservers/codebase_reviewer_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": {
        "REVIEWERS_FILE": "",
        "MAX_REVIEWERS": "3",
        "MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS": "3",
        "QDRANT_URL": "http://localhost:6333",
        "QDRANT_API_KEY": ""
      }
    }
  }
}
